# RecordTwin Dashboard — UX Architecture & Action Mapping

---

## Section 1: Carousel Strategy

The Carousel is prime real estate — the first thing the user's eyes hit after the header. It must show **contextually urgent, time-sensitive information**, not static data the user can find elsewhere. Based on the full requirements analysis:

### Keep
- **Sync Status Dock** — This is the heartbeat of the app. The Split-Sync pipeline (F8) has TWO independent sync channels (automatic text sync + manual image sync). This dock must show:
  - Text sync progress (automatic, background)
  - Image upload queue count + "Sync Images" trigger button (manual, user-initiated)
  - The "X images not backed up" persistent badge (F9) lives here naturally
  - **Why:** Users on expensive prepaid data need to see exactly what's consuming bandwidth at all times. This is the #1 anxiety point for the target demographic.

- **Critical Alerts Dock** — Non-dismissable, escalating system warnings. Specific alerts from the requirements:
  - Storage pre-purge warning: *"These documents will lose their local images"* with Confirm/Cancel (F9)
  - 7-day un-synced image warning — non-dismissable (F9)
  - Pinned storage overflow: *"Your pinned images are consuming too much space"* (F9)
  - AI text-washing completion notification (F15)
  - Sync conflict alert — 409 Conflict requiring merge/override decision (Section 6.2)
  - **Why:** These are time-critical actions that require user decision. Burying them in a notification list means they get ignored. Putting them front-and-center in the carousel forces acknowledgement.

### Remove
- **Data Graphs Dock** — Remove from MVP. The app is a document vault, not an analytics dashboard. There is no feature in the entire master architecture that produces graph-worthy data. The Wheel Picker we built in the HTML mock was a design exploration, but it has no real data source behind it.
  - **Why:** Adding graphs just to fill space violates the Ultra-Minimalist principle. The carousel should only hold items that demand attention.

### Add (New)
- **Onboarding Tips Dock (First 3 Days Only)** — Based on F15's "First 3 Days Rule" and F16's "Smart Empty State":
  - Show contextual tips in Urdu: *"آواز سے لکھیں"* (Dictate with voice), *"تصویر لگائیں"* (Attach an image)
  - Auto-dismiss after 3 days of install, replaced by Sync Status as default dock
  - **Why:** New users face a blank screen. This carousel dock acts as an interactive guide during the critical first-72-hours retention window.

### Final Carousel Dock Order (Priority)
1. **Critical Alert** (auto-opens if any alert exists on app launch — highest priority)
2. **Sync Status** (auto-opens if sync is active and no critical alert exists)
3. **Onboarding Tips** (only during first 3 days, lowest priority)

